  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "my game seems to disconnect \"randomly\" from lobbies. i haven't been able to pinpoint the exact reason why (or how to reproduce it, because other people don't have this issue), but it most often happens on lobbies with high player counts and join / leave activity (like the great pug, where i will disconnect every 2 - 3 minutes if there is high activity). i have also observed that reducing avatars visible / preventing them from being loaded (via the avatar load distance setting) seems to make it disconnect less somehow?\n\ni play on Steam via Steam Link (my headset is a Quest 2), and my PC has a Ryzen 5600 and a AMD Radeon RX7600 XT. i attached a log below where i reproduced a disconnect, clicked \"ok\" on the disconnect alert, and then exited steam vr. the disconnect here happened shortly after i joined a great pug lobby. this issue has been happening for... a few months? i can't exactly remember when, but i only am bothering to report this because i thought it was an issue with my setup, but i tried everything and i don't think it is.",
